## Resolved mutable: joiner-cant-play-rootcause

client/app.js:342 host bridge `bridge.data.addEventListener('peer-open', ({detail})=>{ const dc=bridge.data.peers.get(detail.peerPubkey)?.dc; if(dc) client.attachWireweavePeer(detail.peerPubkey,dc) })` has NO catch-up loop over already-open peers. Contrast client/WireweaveJoinClient.js connect(): after addEventListener('peer-open',onPeerOpen) it runs `for (const [pk,peer] of this._bridge.data.peers) if (peer?.dc?.readyState==='open') { onPeerOpen({detail:{peerPubkey:pk}}); break }`. Host missing that loop => if joiner dc opens before host attaches listener, or peer-open fires with dc still null, host never calls attachWireweavePeer => worker WorkerEntry.js:100 PEER_CONNECT never posted => ServerHandlers onClientConnect never spawns joiner player => joiner appears (nostr presence) but gets no HANDSHAKE_ACK/snapshots and cannot play.